    <h2>A Layered Cup, Not a Blizzard</h2>
<p>What truly sets the Cupfection apart from a standard <a href="/items/oreo-blizzard">Oreo Blizzard</a> is its structural craftsmanship. While a Blizzard is thoroughly whipped for uniform consistency throughout, the Cupfection is deliberately layered like an artisanal parfait. Each spoonful offers a different discovery—a cool bite of soft serve followed by crunchy Oreo crumble, gooey chocolate sauce, or a dense pocket of baked brownie. It's built for those who prefer dynamic texture over blended smoothness.</p>
<h2>Is It Worth $6.29?</h2>
<p>At $6.29 and 820 calories, this treat commands a premium price tag within the classic dessert lineup. For comparison, the beloved <a href="/items/peanut-buster-parfait">Peanut Buster Parfait</a> is priced around $4.99 and 710 calories. You're investing an extra dollar and change specifically for the luxury duo of baked brownies and chocolate sandwich cookies. If you're a devoted chocolate-bakery enthusiast, every bite justifies the upgrade.</p>
<h2>Sharing and Portion Notes</h2>
<p>Because of its dense 820-calorie footprint, many guests find the Cupfection wonderfully suitable for sharing with a friend or partner. Furthermore, because it's served in an upright cup with a lid option, it travels much more cleanly in a car than delicate cones or a wide <a href="/items/banana-split">Banana Split</a> boat. If you ever prefer this exact taste profile in a blended treat, simply request an Oreo Blizzard with extra brownie chunks folded in.</p>
